 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? That's the paint cracking. Light reflects off the cracked surface, so the paint looks darker than it actually is. It' easier to fix than you' think. Sand the damaged areas with 180 grit sandpaper, wipe with rubbing alcohol, yes. Mix a very thin coat of clear coat with a touch of rubbing compound, and apply it to a small area. If it' gone in two days, it' fix it. Use a really good quality gloss enamel, they' designed so the colors never fade.",
